      "note": "First project parser/load step for the vulnerable BAM record. `bam_read1()` reads the first record header from the attacker-controlled stream and materializes the record length and BAM core fields that drive the vulnerable path: `block_len = 73`, `l_qname = 16`, `n_cigar = 2`, and `l_qseq = 10` for the staged witness.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "sam.c",
      "function": "bam_read1",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (bgzf_read(fp, b->data, c->l_qname) != c->l_qname) return -4;",
      "note": "Root cause. After reading `c->l_qname` bytes of qname data into `b->data`, the vulnerable code never checks whether `b->data[c->l_qname - 1]` is `\\0` before the record is later exposed via `bam_get_qname(b)`. The fixing patch inserts exactly that missing post-read validation and repair immediately after this statement.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
